.TH MAIZE 1 "2026-07-30" "Maize" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
maize \- generate and migrate optimized Gentoo kernel configurations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B maize
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B maize
combines Linux kernel configuration, hardware evidence, and Gentoo package
policy to explain, check, migrate, and generate kernel configurations.
It is intended only for Gentoo systems.
.PP
Text output uses color automatically on terminals. Set
.B NO_COLOR
or use
.B --color never
to disable it. JSON output never contains terminal escape sequences.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B inspect
Inspect the selected kernel configuration, current hardware, installed package
state, and package kernel policy. Use
.B --verbose
to print every unresolved policy finding.
.TP
.B generate
Create a target-validated kernel configuration. Requires
.B --kernel-tree
and
.BR --output .
The target kernel's Kconfig evaluator runs against a temporary configuration;
the source tree is not modified.
.TP
.B migrate
By default, compare the running kernel configuration with the result of
migrating it through the newest installed source tree below
.IR /usr/src .
The report identifies both releases and the selected source. Supplying all four
old/new Kconfig and configuration options retains explicit artifact comparison.
The default text report groups consequences and caps large groups. Use
.B --verbose
to include every change, including inactive symbol churn. JSON includes the
complete classified change set.
.TP
.B check
Check known required kernel capabilities. Exit status 3 indicates known
required changes; status 4 indicates that unresolved package policy makes the
result indeterminate.
.TP
.B impact
Report known requirements that a proposed
.B --config
does not satisfy. Consumer-oriented impact analysis is still under development.
.TP
.B observe
Write the current hardware inventory as versioned JSON. Requires
.BR --output .
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --color " " auto|always|never
Control terminal color. The default is
.BR auto .
.TP
.BR --config " " PATH
Use an explicit Linux kernel configuration.
.TP
.BR --format " " text|json
Select human-readable or versioned machine-readable output.
.TP
.BR --root " " PATH
Inspect an alternate Gentoo installation root.
.TP
.BR --snapshot-consistency " " locked|stabilized
Use Portage locks or a lockless stabilized snapshot.
.TP
.B --verbose
Show detailed unresolved package-policy evidence or the complete migration
change stream.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully and, for
.BR check ,
known requirements are satisfied.
.TP
.B 1
Execution or validation failed.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage was invalid.
.TP
.B 3
.B check
found required kernel changes.
.TP
.B 4
.B check
could not reach a definitive result because package kernel policy remains
unresolved.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable color when
.B --color
is
.BR auto .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /proc/config.gz
Preferred running-kernel configuration when no explicit config is supplied.
.TP
.I /usr/src/linux/.config
Fallback kernel configuration and common target tree.
.SH SAFETY
Analysis commands are read-only. Commands that write require explicit output
paths and publish files atomically. Kernel validation uses temporary output and
does not modify the selected source tree.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR make (1),
.BR emerge (1),
.BR kernel-config (5)
